style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> coloring methods.\n</p><p>Case 2.2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> 2-by-2 red squares take up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unit grids\n</p><p>Assume the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> 2-by-2 red squares are at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc631d7ae91db64243a6f9f95a1fe1de3c137e7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{11}, C_{12}, C_{21}, C_{22}, C_{23}, C_{32}, C_{33}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"240\" height=\"18\" />. To make sure there are no more 2-by-2 red squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09badb9ac592572c156bce688f4d42ceb9e62da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/27138ff63d72388cad57fea16b43ef0e5f3af671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"17\" /> can't be red. Meaning that there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> coloring method for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09badb9ac592572c156bce688f4d42ceb9e62da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/27138ff63d72388cad57fea16b43ef0e5f3af671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4p